//!
//! # Shell
//!
//! The interactive terminal the boot thread becomes once the kernel is up:
//! a prompt, line editing and a few commands.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name                     | File                 | Purpose                                         |
//! |--------------------------|----------------------|-------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Shell::Terminal::run`   | `terminal.ign`       | the prompt loop, never returns                  |
//! | `Shell::Commands`        | `commands.ign`       | matches a line against `uptime`, `ps`, `threads`, `run NAME` |
//! | `Shell::ThreadCommands`  | `thread_commands.ign`| the `ps` table and the `threads` demo           |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! `Shell` is at the top of the kernel: it imports whatever a command needs
//! and nothing imports it except `main`.
//!
//! | Imports   | Why                                                                |
//! |-----------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Drivers` | the console, the keyboard decoder                                  |
//! | `Lib`     | the scancode ring buffer the keyboard interrupt fills              |
//! | `Arch`    | `cli`, `sti`, `hlt` around the empty-queue check                   |
//! | `Time`    | `uptime`                                                           |
//! | `Sched`   | `ps` and the demo threads                                          |
//! | `Proc`    | `run NAME` starts a program from a Limine module                   |

import _ from "./commands";
import _ from "./terminal";
import _ from "./thread_commands";

/// Aggregate namespace of the shell. The files above contribute
/// `Shell::Terminal`, `Shell::Commands` and `Shell::ThreadCommands`.
export namespace Shell {}
